      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T17:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m sending this out now since it\u0027s a meaty review. There is some staging prep work still needed around supporting the uncropped tiling that will be done in a parent CL.\n\nThe gold diffs all look okay (minor or explainably more correct, see notes below). Other than dealing with the uncropped tiling case, clients all look good but will likely require rebaselines in chrome. Will re-evaluate that once the legacy crop mode is supported again.",
      "revId": "593939f0a34382fa415f680d753963eb59195e06",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82f64e21_a408c058",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T17:46:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oops, I missed commenting about some of the GM changes:\n\n- the backdrop_imagefilter_croprect family of GMs seems to have improved; it looks like the originally \"correct\" images had some imperceptible transparency to them that is now not present, so arguably the new behavior is better.\n- imagefiltersblurrepeat_unclipped had not been rendering correctly, it was only seeing the red portion of the image instead of all of it. Now the non-intersecting clip is filled with the expected purple.\n- All DDL configs have had churn, but they never really drew correctly before anyways. The imagefilter pipeline hasn\u0027t been conveying content bounds fully through the layer and rendering functions so the DDL boundaries end up creating somewhat clunky and incorrect clips. This blur CL is one of the last dependencies on fixing up that data flow, though, and then I will revisit any other issues causing the DDL cases to render incorrectly.",
      "revId": "593939f0a34382fa415f680d753963eb59195e06",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6d5d54d_311ecb38",
        "filename": "src/effects/imagefilters/SkBlurImageFilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T17:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SkMatrixConvolutionImageFilter was able to be updated to strictly require a crop rect for non-decal tilemodes.\n\nWhile I\u0027ve updated GMs to provide a crop rect in all cases, we have `modules/sksg` and `modules/jetski` that rely on the legacy behavior of tiling when there was an undefined crop rect. All major clients appear to have relied on this behavior as well (g3, chrome, flutter, and Android). \n\nI am going to add an unbounded \"crop\"+tile mode to `SkCropImageFilter` to support this legacy case, and then rebase this CL on top of it. When that is done, the only change should be this `if` in the factory. The rest of the bounds and filtering logic in SkBlurImageFilter can stay unaware of the cropping details.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 116,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "593939f0a34382fa415f680d753963eb59195e06",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b7e7535_081a0994",
        "filename": "src/effects/imagefilters/SkBlurImageFilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T17:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A number of GMs behavior has actually changed because of this. Since tilemodes used to be applied to whatever the source image ended up as, the decal tiling was applied to the input image too. In practice I haven\u0027t seen it causing problems/significant differences for clients and I think only cropping the output better matches how every other image filter behaves. This means that a number of gold diffs (imagefilterscroped, imagefilterscropexpand in particular) now show the source image being expanded with offscreen content to be filtered and then cropped with a harder edge than before.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 116,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "593939f0a34382fa415f680d753963eb59195e06",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
