      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T17:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously, `onFilterImage()` was calculating an output image size that included the radius outset for both X and Y axes. The extra data would be clipped out visually when drawn, but somewhat hid the fact that the CPU blur needed to allocate its output image with storage for the Y pass or it wouldn\u0027t have those offscreen rows available. The GPU blur already does this outset when it creates a GrSurfaceContext for the X pass, so it was actually calculating image sizes that were doubly-outset in the Y axis.\n\nNow that `onFilterImage()` is tightly calculated, this adjusts the CPU allocation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 814,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 814,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "593939f0a34382fa415f680d753963eb59195e06",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
