        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T17:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As noted in an earlier comment, this does lead to more correctness for CPU blurs and some GPU blurs. However, it may also lead to performance regressions. \n\nIn some metal captures, the new code does seem to use fewer render passes overall (because of sticking to FilterResult more than before), but the surfaces for those passes were larger because they included the sigma outset region that held the pixel data of the evaluated tile mode.\n\nI have plans to follow this up to have imageAndOffset() return a tilemode that can be used to sample the returned image, which would further reduce the number of render passes and bring their size back to the current texture sizes. However, this would require the CPU shaders to handle more than kDecal.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 973,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 975,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "593939f0a34382fa415f680d753963eb59195e06",
